{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/4","id":4898981630,"node_id":"PR_kwDON1sLX88AAAABJACG_g","html_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/4","diff_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/4.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/4.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/4","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/4/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/4/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/4/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/statuses/c2da69c3497693c664a21ee5550cd865b79c2bb0","number":4,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix CI/CD warnings, false negatives and vulnerabilities (CRA → Vite, template best practices)","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nFixes #3\n\nBoth `main` runs were green, but their logs had a lot of problems that never failed the build. This PR fixes all of them.\n\n- **Warnings:** the `actions/*@v4` actions still ran on the deprecated Node.js 20 runtime. Every `npm ci` printed 48 `npm warn deprecated` lines. The Create React App build printed the \"Browserslist data is 21 months old\" warning, and `git init` inside checkout printed its \"initial branch name\" hint.\n- **Errors that never failed the build:** `npm ci` reported 107 vulnerabilities (4 critical) and nothing acted on it.\n- **Missing checks:** there was no linting, formatting, file-size, secret, dependency-audit or workflow-lint check.\n- **Misleading green runs and deploy risks:** a deploy on `main` could be cancelled by a newer push. The deploy job built the site a second time instead of publishing the build the tests had checked. The deploy push failed if `main` moved in the meantime.\n\n### Changes\n- **Create React App → Vite 8 + Vitest 5.** `react-scripts` is deprecated, and it is where the vulnerabilities and deprecation warnings came from. Files that contain JSX are renamed to `.jsx`, `index.html` is moved to the repo root, and the build still goes to `build/`.\n- **Workflow:** Node 24 versions of the actions (`checkout@v6`, `setup-node@v6`, `upload/download-artifact`), Node 24 runtime, read-only `permissions` by default, `persist-credentials: false` except in the deploy job, the `init.defaultBranch` env setting, an `actionlint` job, and a `checks` job (ESLint `--max-warnings=0`, Prettier, a 1500-line file limit, secretlint, `npm audit`). Only pull-request runs get cancelled now. The deploy job publishes the tested build artifact and retries the push with a rebase.\n- Pre-commit hook (husky + lint-staged), `.prettierrc`, `eslint.config.js`, `.secretlintrc.json`, all taken from the template.\n- `App.css` (1387 lines) is split into three files imported in the same order. The built CSS is byte-identical (same hash).\n- `src/workflow.test.js`: new policy tests for job timeouts, permissions, Node 24 actions, checkout credentials, deploys not being cancelled, and deploying the tested build.\n\n### Analysis\nThe full analysis is in `dev/log/issues/3/pulls/4/README.md`: requirements, comparison with the template, mapping to the CI/CD best practices, alternatives, and the logs before and after. None of the problems found here exist in the template, so nothing was reported there.\n\n### Verification\n- Locally: `npm run check` passes, `npm run test:ci` passes 34/34, `npm run build` works, `npm audit` reports 0 vulnerabilities, and actionlint 1.7.12 reports nothing.\n- CI run [39022132481](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/actions/runs/39022132481) is green, with 0 warnings, 0 deprecations and 0 vulnerabilities in its logs.\n\n<!-- hive-mind:requirements:start -->\n```json\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"headSha\": \"03ac4ae2e153ab13992ba325fdfedc4cc1f69bc3\",\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"owner\": \"konard\",\n      \"repo\": \"konard.github.io\",\n      \"number\": 3,\n      \"sourceDigest\": \"419b43afebb8d9d3a20a0d50ba45ba8602f6b1bc2c308b1b05202fab70f983fa\",\n      \"requirements\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Inventory every requirement in the issue description and feedback, including prose.\",\n          \"status\": \"done\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Requirements table R1\\u2013R8 in https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-3-b37046349f28/dev/log/issues/3/pulls/4/README.md; issue has no comments, PR has no review feedback\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Check CI/CD for warnings and fix them all\",\n          \"status\": \"done\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Baseline run 39021305360 had Node 20 action warnings, 48 npm deprecations, Browserslist and punycode warnings; after-run 39022132481 log (dev/log/issues/3/pulls/4/ci-logs/run-39022132481-after.log) has none: actions bumped to Node 24 majors, CRA replaced by Vite 8/Vitest 5\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Check CI/CD for errors and fix them all\",\n          \"status\": \"done\",\n          \"evidence\": \"npm audit 107 vulnerabilities -> 0 (gated by `npm audit --audit-level=moderate` in checks job); deploy push gained rebase-and-retry\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Check for false negatives and fix them\",\n          \"status\": \"done\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Added actionlint, ESLint --max-warnings=0, Prettier check, file-size limit, secretlint, npm audit gates; workflow policy tests in src/workflow.test.js (34/34 tests pass)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Check for false positives and fix them\",\n          \"status\": \"done\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Deploy job now publishes the tested build artifact instead of rebuilding; main deploys no longer cancelled (cancel-in-progress only for PRs); App.css split to keep file-size gate warning-free (identical built CSS hash)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Compare all files with js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template and reuse best practices\",\n          \"status\": \"done\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Full template tree in dev/log/issues/3/pulls/4/data/template-file-tree.txt; applied/not-applicable comparison in README.md section 'Template comparison'\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"If the same issue is found in the template, report it there too\",\n          \"status\": \"done\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Compared: template already uses Node 24 actions, persist-credentials false, actionlint, audit; none of this repo's issues exist there, so no report was needed (documented as R7)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Follow hive-mind CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md\",\n          \"status\": \"done\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Section-by-section mapping in README.md 'Best practices mapping'; snapshot in data/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Collect data and analysis into ./dev/log/issues/3/pulls/4\",\n          \"status\": \"done\",\n          \"evidence\": \"dev/log/issues/3/pulls/4/ contains README.md, data/, ci-logs/\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Do everything in this single pull request\",\n          \"status\": \"done\",\n          \"evidence\": \"All commits are on PR #4 branch issue-3-b37046349f28; CI run 39022132481 green\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n<!-- hive-mind:requirements:end -->\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-17T09:33:29Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T11:45:07Z","closed_at":"2026-10-17T11:45:07Z","merged_at":"2026-10-17T11:45:07Z","merge_commit_sha":"dbbf97ee5d8899c91382b4ecf04648fbd57a02f0","assignee":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}"